factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 7 problems
  The article says the weekly market (வாரச்சந்தை) was being closed for maintenance only for six months (ஆறு மாதத்திற்கு மட்டும்), but the reel_script and caption omit this time period entirely and present the closure as open-ended.
  The reel_script says the Tuesday market 'is closed' (மூடப்பட்டுள்ளது), but the article only says it is under maintenance work; the closure claim is an overstatement not in the article.
  The reel_script says sales of farmers were harmed (விற்பனை பாதிக்கப்பட்டுள்ளதாகக் கூறப்படுகிறது); the article only says their livelihood (வாழ்வாதாரம்) is affected, so 'sales' is an added detail.
  slides_spec hl2 claims '1,300 அட்டைதாரர்கள் பாதிப்பு' (1,300 cardholders affected), but the article only says there are 1,300 cardholders, not that all of them are affected.
  slides_spec slide 'விவசாயிகளின்' contains the line 'ஆறு மாதத்திற்கு வாரச்சந்தை திறக்க வேண்டும்', which frames the six months as the period the market should be opened, a meaning that differs from the article where six months refers to the maintenance closure period.
  The reel_script says the farmers complained that small traders' vegetable shops are causing the harm, but the article's sentence about the outside shops is cut off and the causal link to the harm is not clearly stated, so this is an unsupported cause.
  The slides_spec slide 'ஏன் பாதிப்பு?' says the market is closed due to maintenance work, mixing the 'closure' claim with the maintenance cause; the article does not state the market is closed, only that maintenance work is being carried out.
