  The article text is cut off before stating the reason for the cancellation, but the draft says the auction was cancelled and that ஒப்பந்ததாரர்கள் ஆர்ப்பாட்டம் நடத்தியதாக செய்தி வெளியாகியுள்ளது — the article's visible part only says the administration cancelled the auction without any notice; the protest is mentioned only in the headline/title, not in the visible body, so this claim cannot be verified from the article as provided.
  The caption and reel_script both state the cancellation as 'கூறப்படுகிறது' (reportedly), while the article states it as a fact that the administration cancelled the auction without prior notice; the draft omits the key cause given in the article (no prior notice was given by the union administration), so the important fact of who cancelled it and how is missing from the reel_script.
  The draft reel_script and slides say the auction was 'to be held yesterday morning at 11 am', but the caption's date line '(அக். 30, 2026)' is the posting date, not a claim from the article — this part is acceptable; however the draft says 'ஊராட்சி அறிவித்திருந்தது' (the panchayat had announced) while the article attributes the announcement to a 'ஊராட்சி அறிவிப்பு' and the cancellation to 'ஊராட்சி ஒன்றிய நிர்வாகம்' (the panchayat union administration), so the body of the draft conflates the panchayat with the panchayat union administration as the actor.
